	<!-- Permission usage strings — Apple requires a human-readable
	     reason for every protected capability. The system shows these
	     verbatim in the permission prompt and on the privacy
	     transparency screens, so they must be honest and specific. -->
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Globeskimmers uses your location to find nearby restaurants, ATMs, attractions, restrooms, and money exchange spots so we can show you the closest, most relevant results.</string>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Globeskimmers uses your camera to scan price tags for instant currency conversion and to translate signs, menus, and labels into your language.</string>
	<key>NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Globeskimmers uses your photo library so you can save translation screenshots and scanned prices for offline reference.</string>

	<!-- App Tracking Transparency (iOS 14+). Required when an SDK in the
	     app could request the IDFA to personalize ads. The Google Mobile
	     Ads SDK calls ATTrackingManager when this string is present;
	     without it, the App Store can reject the build for "missing ATT
	     usage description even though an ad SDK is bundled." The text
	     here is shown verbatim in the system prompt the first time
	     personalized ads are about to be served. -->
	<key>NSUserTrackingUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Globeskimmers uses this to show ads that are more relevant to you. Choosing "Ask App Not to Track" still shows ads — just less personalized ones.</string>

	<!-- Google Mobile Ads SDK — App ID (Globeskimmers iOS). NOT secret;
	     this identifier ships in every installed binary and is how
	     AdMob attributes ad revenue to your account. Without this key,
	     the SDK crashes the app on launch. -->
	<key>GADApplicationIdentifier</key>
	<string>ca-app-pub-2858807823087664~5847327858</string>

